# Files that live in the repo but must NOT be uploaded to the deployment.
# The repo tree IS the site, so anything here would otherwise be served —
# and fetchable — at https://isaacperez.co/<path>.

# Repo-only docs. The operating manual and the generated atlas name the Vercel
# project/team, the local machine layout and the fleet CI wiring; none of that
# is part of the website.
AGENTS.md
CLAUDE.md
docs/

# The August-2020 student résumé. AGENTS.md keeps it in the repo and unlinked;
# it carries a personal phone number, so it must not sit at a guessable URL.
Resume.pdf

# The retired office game. AGENTS.md keeps js/game.js and css/game.css on disk
# for a possible revival and forbids touching css/rpg.css at all, but nothing
# deployed has loaded any of them since the office was removed — and game.js
# still carries the 0–100 numeric self-ratings and the "Licensed pilot" line the
# homepage stopped showing, so it must not stay fetchable.
js/game.js
css/game.css
css/rpg.css

# The product app icons from the retired apps catalogue. Zero references in any
# deployed HTML, CSS or JS (the employer marks and the portrait live at the root
# and are still used), so they are repo-only too.
images/

# The code face. No deployed page sets type in it any more (/shootsort/'s folder
# tree and 404.html's label use installed monospace), but docs/og/cards.html --
# repo-only, and the source the three share cards are shot from -- still
# @font-faces it so a re-shoot reproduces the committed og-shootsort.png. Repo
# copy stays; nothing on the site requests it, so it must not be fetchable.
fonts/jetbrains-mono-latin.woff2

# The fleet design system. It is byte-identical to the copies in CapturedByIP,
# TeamUp/web and CurbSide/web, so it stays here unedited -- but no page on this
# site links it any more: the four legal pages use its tokens through
# css/legal.css and none of its components. Relink it (and delete this line in
# the same commit) if a page here ever needs .btn/.card/.nav.
css/design-system.css
